    "body": "Jeff Killeen, PDAC's director of policy and programs. Credit: PDAC\nPosted By: Adrian Pocobelli November 11, 2026\nThis week on The Northern Miner Podcast, host Adrian Pocobelli speaks with Jeff Killeen , PDAC’s senior director of policy and programs, about what Canada’s federal budget, tabled Nov. 5, means for mineral exploration.\nKilleen explains why flow-through shares matter to junior explorers and what a proposed multiyear extension of the Mineral Exploration Tax Credit could mean for the sector. He also discusses policy changes that could help companies bridge the “valley of death,” the financing gap between exploration and mine development, and shares what he expects from the 2027 PDAC convention.\nAll this and more with host Adrian Pocobelli.\n“Rattlesnake Railroad”, “Big Western Sky”, “Western Adventure” and “Battle on the Western Frontier” by Brett Van Donsel ( ⁠www.incompetech.com⁠ ).\nLicensed under Creative Commons: By Attribution 4.0 License\n⁠creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0⁠\nApple Podcasts: ⁠ https://podcasts.apple.com/ca/podcast/the-northern-miner-podcast/id1099281201⁠\nSpotify: ⁠ https://open.spotify.com/show/78lyjMTRlRwZxQwz2fwQ4K⁠\nYouTube: ⁠ https://www.youtube.com/@NorthernMiner⁠\nSoundcloud: ⁠ https://soundcloud.com/northern-miner\nThe Northern Miner · PDAC’s Jeff Killeen on what Canada’s budget means for mineral exploration\nPrint\nTAG: Podcast\nRepublish this article",
